🧠 Core Philosophy Shift
We are pivoting from a "Second Brain/Inbox" (which implies work/organizing) to an "Ambient Memory Layer".

Old Way: Save -> Organize -> Search.
New Way: Save -> Forget -> Resurfacing.
Key Promise: No admin work. No "inbox zero". No guilt.
🛠️ Key Feature Changes (The "V1 Upgrade")
We are adding exactly 3 mechanics to the existing MVP:

The Working Set (Recently Relevant)
A visually distinct "top layer" in the Stream.
Shows ~7 items that are "active" in your brain right now.
Driven by: Recent captures + Implicit signals (clicks, copies, views).
Not manual: Users cannot "pin" or "clear" these.
Recall Trigger (The "Aha" Moment)
Search isn't just filtering anymore.
It proactively suggests: "You've seen things like this before".
Surfaces 2-3 items based on heuristics (keywords/context) before the standard results.
Meaning Signal (The Invisible Brain)
We track an invisible "importance score" for every item.
Increases with: Views, copies, repeat captures.
Decays with: Time.
This score powers the Working Set ranking.
🎨 UI/UX Overhaul
Rename: "Inbox" is dead. It is now "The Stream".
Visuals:
Stream: Continuous flow, no hard pages, no item counts ("You have 34 items" is forbidden).
Items: Look like "memory fragments" (minimal), not "cards" or "tasks". No checkboxes, no "mark as read".
Search: Placeholder becomes "What are you thinking about?".
Vibe: Peaceful. If you ignore it for 2 weeks, you shouldn't feel "behind".

Database: Add importance_score and interaction tracking (last_viewed, copy_count).
Logic: Implement the scoring algorithm (decay + interaction boosts).
Frontend: Rebuild 
InboxPage
 into StreamPage with the new 2-section layout (Working Set + Timeline).
Search API: Update to return "Recall" suggestions + standard matches.

